        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Parasol of crochet bobbin lace and silk, and cardboard box, made by W & J Sangster, England, ca. 1860"@en , "Parasol, box and lid. Parasol with a white crochet bobbin lace cover and lined with green silk. Stick and hanging ring of ivory. Silver band is marked 'SANGSTERS'.\n\nBox of cardboard decorated with embroidered scraps and cut gilt paper, and with a label reading 'W & J SANGSTER 140 REGENT St.'"@en ;
